      "title": "Assertions vs Types: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Assertions vs Types: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Assertion vs Annotation",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`x as T` says =={trust me}== to the compiler",
                "Changes the **static type** only",
                "Emits ==no runtime code==: no conversion, no check",
                "A wrong assertion is a {red:runtime crash}, not a compile error"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Annotation",
                "Assertion"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Syntax",
                  "`const a: T = v`",
                  "`v as T`"
                ],
                [
                  "Checker",
                  "**checks** v against T",
                  "**overrides** it"
                ],
                [
                  "Wrong type",
                  "{green:compile error}",
                  "{red:runtime crash}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What `as` Allows",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Allowed only if one type is ==assignable to the other== (they overlap)",
                "No overlap: error. `as unknown as T` forces it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const s = 'a'",
                "// s as number  -> error, no overlap",
                "const n = s as unknown as number"
              ],
              "note": "compiles, but n is still a string at runtime"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Safe Uses",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Safe}: narrow a wider type to a known subtype",
                "`document.getElementById('a') as HTMLInputElement`",
                "{green:Safe}: upcasting, always",
                "`<T>x` is equivalent but ==invalid in .tsx==: use `as`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`as` is a promise, not a conversion. Break it and TypeScript stays silent; the **runtime** pays."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Unsafe Assertions and the Non-Null Operator",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Unsafe Assertions and the Non-Null Operator",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Literal and double assertions",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`{} as User` ==silences== missing-property errors",
                "`user.name.length` then throws at runtime",
                "Prefer a typed annotation or `Partial<User>`",
                "`x as unknown as T` skips overlap checks: {red:last resort}"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The non-null `!`",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`x!` strips `null | undefined` at ==compile time only==",
                "`x!.foo` still throws a **TypeError** if `x` is null",
                "Prefer `?.`, `??`, or an explicit `if (x)`",
                "Keep `!` for facts the compiler can't see"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "if (map.has(k)) {",
                "  const v = map.get(k)!;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "valid use: has() just proved it"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Unvalidated data",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`JSON.parse(s) as User` is unsafe",
                "`(await res.json()) as T` is unsafe too",
                "==No validation== happens at runtime",
                "Validate with a type guard or zod"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`as` and `!` only change the **type**. The runtime value is never checked."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "as const and Literal Types",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "as const and Literal Types",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Widening",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`let x = 'a'` widens to ==string==",
                "`const x = 'a'` keeps the literal `'a'`",
                "Object properties widen even with const: `{ mode: 'dark' }` has `mode: string`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. as const",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Value",
                "Plain",
                "as const"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`['a','b']`",
                  "`string[]`",
                  "`readonly ['a','b']`"
                ],
                [
                  "`{ mode: 'dark' }`",
                  "`mode: string`",
                  "`readonly mode: 'dark'`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const ROLES = ['admin','user'] as const;",
                "type Role = (typeof ROLES)[number];"
              ],
              "note": "Role is 'admin' | 'user'"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Compile-time only: it does not call `Object.freeze`",
                "Literal expressions only, not variables or function calls"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Widened Arguments",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const req = { method: 'GET' } as const;",
                "send(req.method); // param: 'GET' | 'POST'"
              ],
              "note": "Without as const, method is string and this errors"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Fix the value",
              "text": "Put `as const` on the value. Do not assert `as 'GET'`: that skips the check."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "satisfies vs Annotation vs as",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "satisfies vs Annotation vs as",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What satisfies Does",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`expr satisfies T` (TS 4.9+) ==checks== expr against T",
                "It keeps the expression's own ==narrower inferred type==",
                "Typos and missing keys still {red:error}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Annotation vs satisfies vs as",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Checks?",
                "Resulting type"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Annotation `: T`",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "**widens** to T"
                ],
                [
                  "`as T`",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "overrides to T"
                ],
                [
                  "`satisfies T`",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "**keeps narrow**"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "type Colors = Record<'red' | 'green', string | [number, number, number]>;",
                "const c = {",
                "  red: [255, 0, 0],",
                "  green: '#0f0',",
                "} satisfies Colors;",
                "c.red.map(n => n); // still a tuple-like array"
              ],
              "note": "annotation `const c: Colors` would lose `red`'s array type"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`satisfies` {green:catches} excess properties in literals",
                "`as` {red:silently allows} them"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Combine Them",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const cfg = {",
                "  mode: 'dark',",
                "  ports: [80, 443],",
                "} as const satisfies Config;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`as const satisfies Config` = ==readonly==, narrow, and **validated** against Config."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "unknown vs any and Type Guards vs Assertions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "unknown vs any and Type Guards vs Assertions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. any vs unknown",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "any",
                "unknown"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Assign to / from",
                  "everything",
                  "assign to it only"
                ],
                [
                  "Property or call",
                  "{red:allowed}",
                  "{green:error until narrowed}"
                ],
                [
                  "Spreads",
                  "silently",
                  "no"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Narrowing unknown",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Narrow with ==typeof==, ==instanceof==, ==in==",
                "Custom guard: `x is User`",
                "Wrong predicate **lies** to the compiler"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "function isUser(x: unknown): x is User {",
                "  return typeof x === 'object' && x !== null && 'name' in x;",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Guard vs assertion",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Guard",
                "Assertion"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Signature",
                  "`x is T`",
                  "`asserts x is T`"
                ],
                [
                  "On failure",
                  "returns false",
                  "throws"
                ],
                [
                  "Narrows",
                  "inside the if",
                  "code after the call"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule of thumb",
              "text": "Untrusted data (API, JSON, `catch` with `useUnknownInCatchVariables`): guard or validate. Assertion: only for knowledge the compiler can't see. `any`: almost never."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why unknown over any?** It forces narrowing before use.",
                "**Guard vs assertion?** Guard returns boolean; assertion throws."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
